• Failed downloads
• Old APK installers
• Duplicate screenshots
• Temporary exports
• Conversion files
• Empty files
• Broken downloads
• Obsolete generated files

Classify them as:

SAFE
REVIEW
DO NOT TOUCH

Only permanently delete when I have explicitly authorized deletion.

--------------------------------------------------
# 12. APPLICATION-SPECIFIC DIRECTORIES
--------------------------------------------------

Be extremely careful with:

Android/
Android/data/
Android/obb/
Application-managed folders
Messaging databases
Cloud-sync directories
Backup directories

Do not modify these merely to make the folder structure look cleaner.

Never corrupt application data.

Never break synchronization.

--------------------------------------------------
# 13. CLOUD SYNCHRONIZATION
--------------------------------------------------

Before moving a file, determine whether it appears to belong to:

• Google Drive
• OneDrive
• Dropbox
• Other cloud services

Avoid creating unwanted duplicate uploads or sync conflicts.

If moving a cloud-synchronized file could cause unexpected behavior:

STOP THAT OPERATION and report it.

--------------------------------------------------
# 14. CONFIDENCE ENGINE
--------------------------------------------------

Every classification must have a confidence level.

HIGH:
90–100%

MEDIUM:
60–89%

LOW:
Below 60%

HIGH-confidence, non-destructive organization:
→ Perform automatically.

MEDIUM-confidence:
→ Prefer Review unless the action is completely reversible and harmless.

LOW-confidence:
→ Do not move or rename.

Example:

"Aadhaar.pdf"
→ Documents/Government/Identity
→ HIGH confidence

"final_new2.pdf"
→ Unknown
→ LOW confidence
→ Leave untouched

--------------------------------------------------
# 15. EXECUTION MODE
--------------------------------------------------

After authorization, work in this order:

PHASE 1
Inspect device.

PHASE 2
Build internal inventory.

PHASE 3
Classify apps and files.

PHASE 4
Create organization structure.

PHASE 5
Perform SAFE, NON-DESTRUCTIVE organization automatically.

PHASE 6
Verify every operation.

PHASE 7
Present items requiring a decision.

PHASE 8
After separate approval, perform destructive operations such as:

• Permanent deletion
• App uninstall
• Irreversible cleanup

Do NOT stop after Phase 1 asking me for screenshots if you already have device access.

--------------------------------------------------
# 16. VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------

After every batch of operations:

1. Confirm source file existed.
2. Confirm destination exists.
3. Confirm file size is intact.
4. Confirm extension is intact.
5. Confirm file can still be accessed.
6. Confirm no duplicate was accidentally created.
7. Confirm no application appears to be affected.

If verification fails:

STOP that operation.

Do not hide the failure.

--------------------------------------------------
# 17. ROLLBACK
--------------------------------------------------

Maintain an operation log.

For every change record:

Original path
New path
Original name
New name
Timestamp
Action
Result
Confidence

If possible, provide a rollback mechanism for every organization action.

--------------------------------------------------
# 18. DO NOT ASK ME FOR INFORMATION YOU CAN DISCOVER
--------------------------------------------------

This rule is critical.

If you can inspect the phone directly:

DO NOT ASK:

"Please send me your app list."

"Please send screenshots of your folders."

"Please tell me your storage."

"Please list your documents."

"Please upload your Downloads folder."

Instead:

INSPECT THE DEVICE YOURSELF.

Only ask me when:

• Android prevents access
• A permission is required
• There is genuine ambiguity
• An irreversible action requires approval
• Two organizational choices have materially different consequences

